                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "This hands-on workshop will show how to preregister a study on the Open \nScience Framework (OSF), a free, open source project management tool \nthat allows researchers to manage, document, and (optionally) share \ntheir research output with colleagues and the public. You will learn how\n to: (i) choose a template appropriate for your research; (ii) add \nmetadata; (iii) include precise, specific, and exhaustive information in\n the protocol; (iv) upload supplementary files; and (v) make the \npreregistration public (immediately or embargoed)."
                }
              }
            ]
